        "date": "2026-11-15T22:52:20Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): one Weldon holder pick for each taper, the bore from the shank\n\nThe holder picker lists one \"<taper> Weldon\" row for BT30, BT40, CAT40\nand TTS instead of one row for each bore. The pick resolves\n(holder_library::resolve) to the library's existing per-bore entry whose\nbore takes the tool's shank, so the outline, body diameter, fit check and\ncollision bands are exactly the old entry's. SetToolBody::library,\nAddTool's stated holder and the MCP library/holder keys take the grouped\nname too; a shank no standard bore takes is refused by name with the fit\ncheck's text, listing the taper's bores. The data keeps one entry for\neach bore.\n\nFixes #2018\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
